# Line-ending policy. Same convention as the consumer repos: LF everywhere,
# normalized in the repo and checked out as LF on every platform (this
# overrides core.autocrlf).
#
# Here it is not a style preference, it is LOAD-BEARING. The whole
# distribution model is "vendor a byte-identical copy and hash-check it".
# If this repo checked out CRLF on Windows while spec2si-tsmc65 (which pins LF)
# checked out LF, every vendored copy would hash differently on a fresh
# clone and the drift gate would report DRIFTED on files nobody touched --
# a gate that cries wolf is a gate that gets switched off.
#
# Explicit allowlist rather than `* text=auto`, matching the consumer repos.

*.py     text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
